/-!
# Exact cross subtotal of the first two retained runs

The rows are global indices 284 through 479 and the columns are 0 through 96.
Each lower term has weight two. The needed signed sinc entries lie in
[188, 576]. Lean checks the cached row prices and sinc entries against the
literal functions. The column prices reuse the first run's checked table.
The row partition into fourteen intervals limits the size of each kernel
computation without changing any pair or its weight.

The integer data were computed from `scripts/verify_odd_three_sine_hs.py`,
blob `b35434bed50c8a6ba218d01575e1964cae9a93e6`, lines 126–156.
-/

